    pr:source <http://example.org/sen0401/engine/paper#midterm_v3_src2> ;
    pr:stem "Chance, in percent, that an attacker with a share of the hash power ever catches up when a payment has z confirmations: for 10 percent, z = 1 gives 20.5, z = 2 gives 5.1, z = 3 gives 1.3 and z = 6 gives 0.02; for 30 percent, z = 1 gives 62.8, z = 3 gives 32.5, z = 6 gives 13.2, z = 9 gives 5.5 and z = 10 gives 4.2. A shop accepts a payment only when the chance of a reversal is below 5 percent. Tips: confirmation: each further block built on the block that holds a payment; hash power: computing power used to add blocks; attacker: someone who rebuilds the latest blocks to take a payment back. Which statement follows from these figures?" .

