    pr:letter "C" ;
    pr:text "Six confirmations are equally safe against either attacker, because each divides the chance equally." .

<http://example.org/sen0401/engine/paper#midterm_v3_item2_optD> pr:isKey false ;
    pr:letter "D" ;
    pr:text "Two confirmations are enough against the 10 percent attacker, because z = 2 is below 5 percent." .

<http://example.org/sen0401/engine/paper#midterm_v3_item3> a pr:ChoiceItem,
        pr:Item ;
    en:copyChecked true ;
    en:kind en:Direct ;
    en:normStem "" ;
    en:optionSetKey "itrefusestostartthefileasksforpruningandtheindextogetherwhichclash|itstartswithpruning550noindexandcache2048thecommandlinereplacesthefileandnoindexremovestheclash|itstartswithpruningandtheindexonbecausetherefusalcoversonlythecommandline|itstartswiththeindexonandacacheof450becausethefilereplacesthecommandline" ;
    en:origin en:Authored ;
    en:primaryChapter 3 ;
    en:seedItem <http://example.org/sen0401/engine/page#ch03_question_bank_v1_0_0_json_66>,
        <http://example.org/sen0401/engine/page#ch03_question_bank_v1_0_0_json_68>,
        <http://example.org/sen0401/engine/page#ch03_question_bank_v1_0_0_json_76>,
        <http://example.org/sen0401/engine/page#ch03_quiz_v1_0_0_json_1> ;
    en:tests <http://example.org/sen0401/engine/criticalpoint#CP3.05>,
        <http://example.org/sen0401/engine/criticalpoint#CP3.06> ;
    pr:bloomLevel 4 ;
    pr:chapter 3 ;
    pr:code """# bitcoin.conf
prune=550
txindex=1
dbcache=450
# the command line
bitcoind -txindex=0 -dbcache=2048""" ;
    pr:codeLines 6 ;
    pr:codeMaxColumns 33 ;
    pr:itemKey "mt2:i09:conf-precedence-and-refusal" ;
    pr:itemType pr:ChoiceFourCode ;
    pr:option <http://example.org/sen0401/engine/paper#midterm_v3_item3_optA>,
        <http://example.org/sen0401/engine/paper#midterm_v3_item3_optB>,
        <http://example.org/sen0401/engine/paper#midterm_v3_item3_optC>,
        <http://example.org/sen0401/engine/paper#midterm_v3_item3_optD> ;
    pr:position 3 ;
    pr:source <http://example.org/sen0401/engine/paper#midterm_v3_src3> ;
    pr:stem "A node reads the configuration file and is started with the command line shown. Tips: prune: deletes old block files to save disk; txindex: indexes all transactions; it needs all blocks, which pruning deletes; dbcache and bitcoind: the memory cache size and the node program; command line: options typed at the start; they replace the same options of the file for that run. What happens, and why?" .

<http://example.org/sen0401/engine/paper#midterm_v3_item3_optA> pr:isKey false ;
    pr:letter "A" ;
    pr:text "It starts with pruning and the index on, because the refusal covers only the command line." .

<http://example.org/sen0401/engine/paper#midterm_v3_item3_optB> pr:isKey false ;
    pr:letter "B" ;
    pr:text "It refuses to start: the file asks for pruning and the index together, which clash." .

<http://example.org/sen0401/engine/paper#midterm_v3_item3_optC> pr:isKey false ;
    pr:letter "C" ;
    pr:text "It starts with the index on and a cache of 450, because the file replaces the command line." .

<http://example.org/sen0401/engine/paper#midterm_v3_item3_optD> pr:isKey true ;
    pr:letter "D" ;
    pr:text "It starts with pruning 550, no index and cache 2048: the command line replaces the file, and no index removes the clash." .

